# Every route is prerendered to its own index.html at build time, so there is
# nothing left for an SPA fallback to do. The old rule here was
#   /*    /index.html   200
# which turned every mistyped URL into a soft 404: HTTP 200, carrying the
# homepage's title and "index, follow". Serving the real 404 document with a
# real 404 status is what stops crawlers indexing junk URLs.
#
# Static files and prerendered directories are matched before this rule.
/*    /404.html   404
